  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 1230 AM Saturday...\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1... Unsettled weather expected to start on Sunday and \ncontinue through at least early next week, including periods of \nstrong storms and a localized flooding threat.\n\n\ufeffAn upper low over the Mid-Mississippi Valley region will settle \nsouth-southeast and establish a positively tilted trough over the OH \nValley and Deep South through early in the week.  Deep south-\nsouthwesterly flow downstream of the trough will advect a moist \nairmass across our region, with PW exceeding 2-2.5 inches areawide \nby Sunday as a weak stalled boundary over the Southeast lifts \nthrough the area as a warm front. The better deep moisture will \nshift east by Monday but likely linger over eastern NC through \nmidweek as the upper trough axis slowly shifts east. Forcing for \nshowers and storms is somewhat nebulous, but the pattern favors \nperiodic upper disturbances resulting in scattered to numerous \nshowers and storms and the potential for training and backbuilding \nin relatively unidirectional deep layer flow.  Instability each day \nis also somewhat in question in the moist airmass, but soundings \nsuggest sufficient low-level moisture to promote 500-1000 MLCAPE. \nThus, a conditional flooding threat will likely exist each day \nSunday through Tue/Wed, perhaps greatest areawide on Sunday \nafternoon and evening but also present through the overnight hours \nas well.",
